@page "/semantic-conventions"

<PageTitle>Semantic conventions · Belemetry</PageTitle>

<div class="bb-intro">
    <h1>Semantic conventions</h1>
    <p class="bb-subtitle">
        Belemetry follows the OpenTelemetry data model and its semantic conventions, so a page view, a fetch or an
        exception arrives with the attribute names every OTLP backend already knows how to query. This page is the
        reference: what each record looks like, the resource that describes where it came from, the feature bit it
        belongs to, and what the script keeps in browser storage.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-primary"></span> Feature bits</h3>
    <p>
        Every record belongs to exactly one feature, and is only collected while that feature is both switched on
        by configuration (<code>options.Features</code>) and granted by the user. The numbers are the same in C#
        (<code>BelemetryFeatures</code>) and in the script (<code>Features</code>), and they are what
        <code>BitBelemetry.setConsent</code> takes.
    </p>
    <div class="bb-scroll">
        <table class="bb-table">
            <thead>
                <tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Bit</th><th scope="col">Covers</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>Errors</code></td><td>1</td><td>JS errors and unhandled rejections; .NET logs at Error/Critical or carrying an exception; <code>TrackException</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>PageViews</code></td><td>2</td><td>Page views (history/enhanced navigation, <code>TrackPageView</code>)</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Interactions</code></td><td>4</td><td>Clicks and other user interactions</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Performance</code></td><td>8</td><td>Web vitals (LCP, INP, CLS, FCP, TTFB), document-load span, resource timing, long tasks</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Dependencies</code></td><td>16</td><td>Browser fetch/XHR client spans</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Sessions</code></td><td>32</td><td>A session id that survives reloads (in <code>sessionStorage</code>). Without it, the session id lives in memory only</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>UserTracking</code></td><td>64</td><td><code>enduser.pseudo.id</code> (random id persisted in <code>localStorage</code>) and <code>user.id</code> (authenticated id from <code>SetUserAsync</code> / <code>setUser</code>)</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Logs</code></td><td>128</td><td>.NET logs below Error; browser console capture below error</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Traces</code></td><td>256</td><td>.NET <code>Activity</code> spans</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Metrics</code></td><td>512</td><td>.NET <code>Meter</code> metrics</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Persistence</code></td><td>1024</td><td>Keeping unsent telemetry on the device (<code>localStorage</code> / files) for retry after going offline or reloading</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Events</code></td><td>2048</td><td>Custom events (<code>TrackEvent</code>)</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <div class="bb-scroll">
        <table class="bb-table">
            <thead>
                <tr><th scope="col">Group</th><th scope="col">Value</th><th scope="col">Members</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>Diagnostics</code></td><td>401</td><td>Errors, Logs, Traces, Dependencies</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Analytics</code></td><td>2150</td><td>PageViews, Interactions, Sessions, UserTracking, Events</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Monitoring</code></td><td>520</td><td>Performance, Metrics</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>All</code></td><td>4095</td><td>Every feature</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <ApiTable TypeName="BelemetryFeatures" />
</div>

<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-success"></span> Browser records</h3>
    <p>
        Events are log records with an <code>eventName</code>, the way the OpenTelemetry Events API models them.
        Spans use the OTLP span kinds (1 internal, 2 server, 3 client, 4 producer, 5 consumer) and status codes
        (0 unset, 1 ok, 2 error),
        and log severities use the OTLP <code>SeverityNumber</code>. Times are milliseconds since the Unix epoch,
        from <code>performance.timeOrigin + performance.now()</code>.
    </p>
    <div class="bb-scroll">
        <table class="bb-table">
            <thead>
                <tr><th scope="col">Record</th><th scope="col">Shape</th><th scope="col">Scope</th><th scope="col">Feature</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>Page view</td>
                    <td>Log record, <code>eventName = "browser.page_view"</code>. Attributes: <code>url.full</code>, <code>url.path</code>, <code>page.title</code>, <code>page.referrer</code> (redacted), <code>browser.navigation.type</code> (<code>initial</code>/<code>push</code>/<code>replace</code>/<code>pop</code>/<code>hash</code>/<code>manual</code>/<code>restore</code> - <code>restore</code> is a return from the back/forward cache, which fires no history event)</td>
                    <td><code>bit.belemetry.page_views</code></td>
                    <td>PageViews</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Page visit time</td>
                    <td>Log record, <code>eventName = "browser.page_visit_time"</code>, only with <code>TrackPageVisitTime</code>: emitted for the previous page when the next page view starts, and for the current page when it is hidden. Attributes: <code>url.full</code>, <code>url.path</code>, <code>page.title</code>, <code>page.visit.duration</code> (ms)</td>
                    <td><code>bit.belemetry.page_views</code></td>
                    <td>PageViews</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Click</td>
                    <td>Log record, <code>eventName = "browser.user_interaction"</code>. Attributes: <code>event.type</code>, <code>target.element</code>, <code>target.id</code>, <code>target.name</code> (<code>data-bit-belemetry-name</code>, <code>aria-label</code>, then <code>name</code>), <code>target.text</code> (only with <code>captureText</code>), <code>target.xpath</code>. Elements under <code>[data-bit-belemetry-ignore]</code> are skipped</td>
                    <td><code>bit.belemetry.interactions</code></td>
                    <td>Interactions</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Rage click</td>
                    <td>Log record, <code>eventName = "browser.rage_click"</code>, only with <code>TrackRageClicks</code> (on by default): once per burst of 3 clicks on one element within 1 s. The click's target attributes, <code>event.type = "rage_click"</code>, <code>interaction.click_count = 3</code></td>
                    <td><code>bit.belemetry.interactions</code></td>
                    <td>Interactions</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Web vital</td>
                    <td>Log record, <code>eventName = "browser.web_vital"</code>. Attributes: <code>web_vital.name</code> (<code>LCP</code>/<code>INP</code>/<code>CLS</code>/<code>FCP</code>/<code>TTFB</code>), <code>web_vital.value</code>, <code>web_vital.delta</code>, <code>web_vital.rating</code> (<code>good</code>/<code>needs-improvement</code>/<code>poor</code>), <code>web_vital.id</code>, <code>web_vital.navigation_type</code>. A back/forward-cache restore starts a new generation under new ids, as Google's web-vitals library does: FCP and LCP from the restore to the next painted frame, CLS and INP from zero, navigation type <code>back-forward-cache</code></td>
                    <td><code>bit.belemetry.web_vitals</code></td>
                    <td>Performance</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Document load</td>
                    <td>Internal span <code>documentLoad</code>, with events <code>domInteractive</code>, <code>domContentLoadedEventEnd</code>, <code>loadEventEnd</code>, ... from <code>PerformanceNavigationTiming</code></td>
                    <td><code>bit.belemetry.document_load</code></td>
                    <td>Performance</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Resource timing</td>
                    <td>Internal span <code>resourceFetch</code> with <code>url.full</code>, <code>http.response.body.size</code>, <code>network.protocol.name</code></td>
                    <td><code>bit.belemetry.resources</code></td>
                    <td>Performance</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Long task</td>
                    <td>Internal span <code>longtask</code></td>
                    <td><code>bit.belemetry.long_tasks</code></td>
                    <td>Performance</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>fetch/XHR</td>
                    <td>Client span <code>{METHOD}</code>. Attributes: <code>http.request.method</code>, <code>url.full</code>, <code>server.address</code>, <code>server.port</code>, <code>http.response.status_code</code>, <code>error.type</code>. A method outside the conventions' list is <code>_OTHER</code> (span name <code>HTTP</code>) with <code>http.request.method_original</code>. A request the app aborted keeps <code>error.type = AbortError</code> but no error status; <code>TimeoutError</code>, <code>NetworkError</code> and 4xx/5xx answers are errors. Adds <code>traceparent</code> only for targets matched by <code>propagateTraceContextTo</code></td>
                    <td><code>bit.belemetry.http</code></td>
                    <td>Dependencies</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>JS error</td>
                    <td>Log record, severity 17 (ERROR), <code>eventName = "exception"</code>. Attributes: <code>exception.type</code>, <code>exception.message</code>, <code>exception.stacktrace</code></td>
                    <td><code>bit.belemetry.errors</code></td>
                    <td>Errors</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Console</td>
                    <td>Log record at the console call's level (with <code>captureConsole</code>, for the levels in <code>consoleLevels</code>)</td>
                    <td><code>bit.belemetry.console</code></td>
                    <td>Errors at <code>error</code>, Logs below</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Custom event</td>
                    <td>Log record, <code>eventName</code> = the name passed to <code>trackEvent</code>, with its attributes</td>
                    <td><code>bit.belemetry.events</code></td>
                    <td>Events</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Common (every record)</td>
                    <td><code>session.id</code>. <code>enduser.pseudo.id</code> and <code>user.id</code> only with <code>UserTracking</code></td>
                    <td></td>
                    <td></td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-warning"></span> .NET records</h3>
    <div class="bb-scroll">
        <table class="bb-table">
            <thead>
                <tr><th scope="col">Record</th><th scope="col">Shape</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>ILogger</code> entry</td>
                    <td>
                        Log record with the category as its scope, the severity mapped from the <code>LogLevel</code>, the
                        structured values as attributes, <code>log.event.id</code> and <code>log.event.name</code> (from
                        the <code>EventId</code>, when set), the values of active scopes (<code>Logs.IncludeScopes</code>),
                        <code>log.record.template</code> (with <code>Logs.IncludeMessageTemplate</code>), and the current
                        trace and span id
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>ILogger</code> entry with an exception</td>
                    <td>The same, plus <code>exception.type</code>, <code>exception.message</code>, <code>exception.stacktrace</code> - feature Errors</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>Activity</code></td>
                    <td>A span with the activity's kind, status, tags as attributes, events and links, scoped by its <code>ActivitySource</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>Meter</code> instrument</td>
                    <td>Counters and up-down counters as sums, histograms with explicit buckets, gauges as last values; past the cardinality limit, an <code>otel.metric.overflow = true</code> point</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>TrackEvent</code> / <code>TrackPageView</code> / <code>TrackException</code></td>
                    <td>The same records as their browser counterparts: an event log record, a <code>browser.page_view</code> log record, an <code>exception</code> log record</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>ASP.NET Core request (server pipeline)</td>
                    <td>Server span <code>{method} {route}</code>: <code>http.request.method</code>, <code>url.scheme</code>, <code>http.route</code>, <code>http.response.status_code</code>, <code>network.protocol.version</code>, <code>error.type</code>, plus <code>url.path</code>, <code>server.address</code> and <code>server.port</code> on .NET 10; a 5xx is an error</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>EF Core command (<code>Bit.Belemetry.EntityFrameworkCore</code>)</td>
                    <td>Client span named after the database: <code>db.system.name</code>, <code>db.namespace</code>, <code>server.address</code>, <code>server.port</code>, <code>efcore.command.source</code>, <code>db.query.text</code> (opt-in), <code>error.type</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Hangfire execution (<code>Bit.Belemetry.Hangfire</code>)</td>
                    <td>Consumer span <code>JOB {Type}.{Method}</code>, parented to the enqueue's trace: <code>job.id</code>, <code>job.type</code>, <code>job.method</code>, <code>job.queue</code>, <code>job.created_at</code>, <code>error.type</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Belemetry's own health (the <code>Bit.Belemetry</code> meter)</td>
                    <td>Counters <code>belemetry.records.dropped</code> (<code>belemetry.reason</code>, <code>belemetry.signal</code>) and <code>belemetry.records.exported</code> (<code>belemetry.exporter</code>, <code>belemetry.outcome</code>) - see <a href="/dotnet">.NET instrumentation</a></td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-primary"></span> Resource attributes</h3>
    <p>
        The resource describes the producer rather than the event, and travels once per batch. The first eight are
        common to both sides; the rest say which side the record came from.
    </p>
    <div class="bb-scroll">
        <table class="bb-table">
            <thead>
                <tr><th scope="col">Attribute</th><th scope="col">Value</th><th scope="col">Side</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>service.name</code></td><td><code>ServiceName</code>, else <code>OTEL_SERVICE_NAME</code>, else the entry assembly name</td><td>both</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>service.version</code></td><td><code>ServiceVersion</code>, else the entry assembly's informational version</td><td>both</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>service.namespace</code></td><td><code>ServiceNamespace</code></td><td>both</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>service.instance.id</code></td><td><code>ServiceInstanceId</code>; else, on a server, the platform's instance name (<code>WEBSITE_INSTANCE_ID</code>, <code>CONTAINER_APP_REPLICA_NAME</code>) or the machine name; else a random id per process, and always a random id per page load in the browser</td><td>both</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>deployment.environment.name</code></td><td><code>Environment</code></td><td>both</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>telemetry.sdk.name</code></td><td><code>bit-belemetry</code></td><td>both</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>telemetry.sdk.language</code></td><td><code>dotnet</code> / <code>webjs</code></td><td>both</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>telemetry.sdk.version</code></td><td>The package version</td><td>both</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>process.runtime.name</code>, <code>.version</code>, <code>.description</code></td><td><code>.NET</code>, the runtime version and framework description</td><td>.NET</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>os.type</code>, <code>os.description</code>, <code>host.arch</code></td><td>The operating system and process architecture</td><td>.NET</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>process.pid</code></td><td>The process id (not in WebAssembly)</td><td>.NET</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>host.name</code>, <code>process.executable.name</code>, <code>process.owner</code></td><td>The machine name, the executable and the account the process runs as (server only - a device's are its owner's)</td><td>.NET</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>container.id</code></td><td>From <code>/proc/self/mountinfo</code> or <code>/proc/self/cgroup</code> (server only, Linux)</td><td>.NET</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>cloud.provider</code>, <code>cloud.platform</code>, <code>cloud.region</code>, <code>cloud.resource_id</code>, <code>host.id</code>, <code>azure.*</code></td><td>Azure App Service, Functions or Container Apps, from their environment variables (server only, with <code>UseEnvironmentVariables</code>)</td><td>.NET</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>browser.language</code>, <code>browser.mobile</code>, <code>browser.platform</code>, <code>browser.brands</code></td><td>From <code>navigator</code> and User-Agent Client Hints, where available</td><td>browser</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>user_agent.original</code></td><td>The user agent string (with <code>Privacy.CollectUserAgent</code>)</td><td>browser</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <p>
        <code>options.ResourceAttributes</code> adds your own, and outside the browser <code>OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES</code>
        is merged in first, so explicit options win.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-success"></span> Browser storage keys</h3>
    <p>Belemetry sets no cookies. These are the only keys it writes, and each one is gated by the feature it serves.</p>
    <div class="bb-scroll">
        <table class="bb-table">
            <thead>
                <tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Storage</th><th scope="col">Gated by</th><th scope="col">Content</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>bit-belemetry-consent</code></td><td>localStorage</td><td>always (strictly necessary: records the choice itself)</td><td><code>{"v":1,"features":&lt;int&gt;,"time":&lt;ms&gt;}</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>bit-belemetry-session</code></td><td>sessionStorage</td><td><code>Sessions</code></td><td><code>{"id":"&lt;32 hex&gt;","start":&lt;ms&gt;,"last":&lt;ms&gt;}</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>bit-belemetry-pseudo-id</code></td><td>localStorage</td><td><code>UserTracking</code></td><td>32 hex chars</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>bit-belemetry-user-id</code></td><td>sessionStorage</td><td><code>UserTracking</code></td><td>authenticated id from <code>setUser</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>bit-belemetry-queue</code></td><td>localStorage</td><td><code>Persistence</code></td><td><code>[{"id","exporter","url","contentType","body"(base64),"time"}]</code>, capped by <code>persistence.maxBytes</code></td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <p>
        Revoking a feature clears its key: <code>Persistence</code> removes the queue, <code>Sessions</code> the stored
        session, and <code>UserTracking</code> the pseudo id and the user id.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-warning"></span> Browser configuration</h3>
    <p>
        <code>&lt;BelemetryScript /&gt;</code> writes this object into
        <code>&lt;script type="application/json" id="bit-belemetry-config"&gt;</code>, built from the server's
        <code>BelemetryOptions</code>, and the module starts from it on load. <code>&lt;BelemetryInitializer /&gt;</code>
        passes the same object to <code>start(config)</code>, which is idempotent. Without .NET, pass it to
        <code>BitBelemetry.start</code> yourself - every field is optional.
    </p>
    <CodeSnippet Code="@ConfigCode" Language="JSON" Expanded="true" />
    <ul class="bb-detail-list">
        <li><code>propagateTraceContextTo</code> entries are <code>"same-origin"</code>, <code>"*"</code>, or a regex source matched against the absolute URL.</li>
        <li><code>ignoreUrls</code> and <code>ignoreMessages</code> are regex sources.</li>
        <li>
            An exporter's <code>endpoint</code> may be relative (<code>BrowserEndpoint = "/otlp"</code>): the script
            resolves it against the page URL, both to post and to recognize its own export requests.
        </li>
        <li>
            <code>headers</code> of an OTLP exporter are its <code>BrowserHeaders</code> alone when a server renders the
            configuration - its <code>Headers</code> are server configuration and never published in a page; in
            WebAssembly and Hybrid they are <code>Headers</code> with <code>BrowserHeaders</code> on top.
        </li>
        <li>
            <code>protocol</code> is never <code>grpc</code>: a page cannot speak it, so a gRPC exporter reaches the
            browser only through its <code>BrowserEndpoint</code>, as <code>http/protobuf</code>, and is left out without one.
        </li>
        <li>
            <code>signals</code> is the exporter's <code>BelemetrySignals</code> restricted to what the browser produces:
            traces 1, logs 2 (web vitals are log records). Absent means both; an exporter with neither is left out.
            Exporters with <code>IncludeInBrowser = false</code> or an <code>AccessTokenProvider</code> are left out too.
        </li>
        <li>
            <code>ignoreUrls</code> lists the .NET exporters' URLs only when the .NET pipeline runs in the page
            (WebAssembly): a server lists none, since its exports never touch the page and it must not publish internal
            collector addresses.
        </li>
        <li>
            <code>service.instanceId</code> is null from <code>&lt;BelemetryScript /&gt;</code>: a browser tab is its own
            instance, so the script generates a random <code>service.instance.id</code> per page load.
        </li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-primary"></span> The constants</h3>
    <p>
        <code>BelemetrySemanticConventions</code> holds every attribute and event name above as a
        <code>const string</code>, for processors and custom exporters that read or write them - so a typo is a
        compile error rather than an attribute nobody queries.
    </p>
    <CodeSnippet Code="@ConstantsCode" Language="C#" />
    <ApiTable TypeName="BelemetrySemanticConventions" Kinds="@(new[] { "Constant" })" />
</div>

@code {
    private const string ConfigCode = """
        {
          "service": { "name": "MyApp", "version": "1.0.0", "namespace": null, "instanceId": null, "environment": "Production" },
          "resource": { "any.attribute": "value" },             // extra resource attributes
          "sdkVersion": "10.6.2",
          "transport": "direct",                                 // "direct" (JS exports itself) | "relay" (JS hands records to .NET)
          "exporters": [
            { "type": "otlp", "endpoint": "http://localhost:4318", "tracesEndpoint": null, "logsEndpoint": null,
              "protocol": "http/protobuf", "headers": { "x-api-key": "..." }, "compression": "none", "signals": 3 },   // protocol: http/protobuf | http/json ; compression: none | gzip
            { "type": "azureMonitor", "connectionString": "InstrumentationKey=...;IngestionEndpoint=https://...", "maskIp": true,
              "compression": "none", "signals": 3 },
            { "type": "console" }
          ],
          "features": 4095,                                      // instrumentations switched on by configuration
          "consent": { "default": 0, "persist": true, "honorGlobalPrivacyControl": true, "pendingLimit": 500 },
          "pageViews": { "trackHashChanges": false, "trackVisitTime": false },
          "interactions": { "events": ["click"], "captureText": false, "maxTextLength": 64, "rageClicks": true },
          "performance": { "webVitals": true, "documentLoad": true, "resources": false, "longTasks": false },
          "dependencies": { "fetch": true, "xhr": true, "propagateTraceContextTo": ["same-origin"], "ignoreUrls": ["/_framework/", "/_blazor", "/_content/"] },
          "errors": { "ignoreMessages": ["ResizeObserver loop", "^Script error\\.?$"], "duplicateWindowMs": 5000, "maxPerMinute": 100 },
          "logs": { "captureConsole": false, "consoleLevels": ["error", "warn"] },
          "privacy": { "redactQueryParameters": ["token","code","password","pwd","secret","key","apikey","api_key","auth","authorization","session","sid","sig","signature","email","access_token","id_token","refresh_token",
